      "id": "6afaca9fb28681ca461e8cad",
      "fieldData": {
       "alpb---prompt": "<p>Build a scored quiz for new hires with 15 questions, where safety questions are worth 2 points and the pass mark is 16 of 20.</p><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbPrompt = {\"default\": \"Build a scored quiz for new hires with 15 questions, where safety questions are worth 2 points and the pass mark is 16 of 20.\", \"chips\": [{\"label\": \"Point Values\", \"add\": \"Add point values so the 5 hardest questions count double.\"}, {\"label\": \"Pass Mark Email\", \"add\": \"Add an email to the trainer that names each person who scores under the pass mark.\"}, {\"label\": \"Partial Credit\", \"add\": \"Add partial credit on select-all questions, one point per correct pick.\"}, {\"label\": \"Score Bands\", \"add\": \"Add a result screen for each score band, with what to review next.\"}]}; </script></div></div><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script id='awb-quiz-data'> window.awbQuiz = {\"version\":1,\"type\":\"knowledge\",\"title\":\"Can You Score This Scored Quiz by Hand?\",\"intro\":\"Eight questions on points, pass marks, wrong-answer penalties, and score bands. Work each one out, then see how your own total lands.\",\"questions\":[{\"text\":\"A 10-question quiz gives 1 point per right answer. A player gets 7 right. What is the score as a percentage?\",\"options\":[{\"text\":\"7 percent\"},{\"text\":\"70 percent\",\"correct\":true},{\"text\":\"75 percent\"},{\"text\":\"80 percent\"}],\"explanation\":\"Divide points earned by points possible and multiply by 100: 7 / 10 x 100 = 70.\",\"derivable\":true},{\"text\":\"A quiz has 12 questions worth 1 point and 4 questions worth 2 points. What is the highest possible score?\",\"options\":[{\"text\":\"16\"},{\"text\":\"18\"},{\"text\":\"20\",\"correct\":true},{\"text\":\"24\"}],\"explanation\":\"The 12 one-point questions give 12, and the 4 two-point questions give 8. 12 + 8 = 20.\",\"derivable\":true},{\"text\":\"On that same 20-point quiz, the pass mark is 80 percent of the points. How many points does a player need to pass?\",\"options\":[{\"text\":\"14\"},{\"text\":\"15\"},{\"text\":\"16\",\"correct\":true},{\"text\":\"18\"}],\"explanation\":\"80 percent of 20 is 0.8 x 20 = 16.\",\"derivable\":true},{\"text\":\"Each right answer earns 1 point and each wrong answer loses 0.25. Blanks score 0. A player has 14 right, 4 wrong, and 2 blank. Score?\",\"options\":[{\"text\":\"12\"},{\"text\":\"13\",\"correct\":true},{\"text\":\"14\"},{\"text\":\"15\"}],\"explanation\":\"14 right gives 14, and 4 wrong take away 4 x 0.25 = 1. The 2 blanks add nothing. 14 - 1 = 13.\",\"derivable\":true},{\"text\":\"A select-all question has 3 right options. A right pick earns 1, a wrong pick loses 1, and 0 is the floor. Picks: 2 right, 1 wrong. Score?\",\"options\":[{\"text\":\"0\"},{\"text\":\"1\",\"correct\":true},{\"text\":\"2\"},{\"text\":\"3\"}],\"explanation\":\"2 right picks earn 2, and the 1 wrong pick takes 1 away. 2 - 1 = 1, which is above the floor of 0.\",\"derivable\":true},{\"text\":\"A 20-point quiz has three result bands: 0 to 9, 10 to 14, and 16 to 20. Which score has no result screen?\",\"options\":[{\"text\":\"9\"},{\"text\":\"10\"},{\"text\":\"15\",\"correct\":true},{\"text\":\"16\"}],\"explanation\":\"The second band ends at 14 and the third starts at 16, so a player who scores exactly 15 falls between them.\",\"derivable\":true},{\"text\":\"Part A has 30 questions worth 1 point. Part B has 10 questions worth 3 points. What share of the total points comes from Part B?\",\"options\":[{\"text\":\"25 percent\"},{\"text\":\"33 percent\"},{\"text\":\"50 percent\",\"correct\":true},{\"text\":\"75 percent\"}],\"explanation\":\"Part A is worth 30 points and Part B is worth 10 x 3 = 30. The total is 60, and 30 / 60 = 0.5, or 50 percent.\",\"derivable\":true},{\"text\":\"Five players score 12, 15, 18, 9, and 16 points. What is the average score?\",\"options\":[{\"text\":\"13\"},{\"text\":\"14\",\"correct\":true},{\"text\":\"15\"},{\"text\":\"16\"}],\"explanation\":\"12 + 15 + 18 + 9 + 16 = 70, and 70 / 5 = 14.\",\"derivable\":true}],\"results\":[{\"key\":\"recount\",\"title\":\"Time for a Recount\",\"description\":\"You scored 0 to 3. Weighted points and penalties are easy to trip on. Before you launch a scored quiz, write the maximum score and the pass mark down and test a perfect run, a zero, and a run that lands exactly on the mark.\",\"min\":0,\"max\":3},{\"key\":\"steady-scorer\",\"title\":\"Steady Scorekeeper\",\"description\":\"You scored 4 to 6. You can add up a weighted quiz, and the misses are in the edge cases: penalties, partial credit, or a gap between bands. Check those three before your quiz goes live.\",\"min\":4,\"max\":6},{\"key\":\"ready-to-run\",\"title\":\"Ready to Run the Scoring\",\"description\":\"You scored 7 or 8. You can weight questions, set a pass mark, and spot a missing band. Put those rules in a prompt, and the quiz you build can do the adding up for every player.\",\"min\":7,\"max\":8}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6afabd0f4fd422c130d19f15",
      "fieldData": {
       "alpb---prompt": "<p>Build a spelling quiz for my third-grade class that grades each typed word and shows me which words to reteach.</p><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbPrompt = {\"default\": \"Build a spelling quiz for my third-grade class that grades each typed word and shows me which words to reteach.\", \"chips\": [{\"label\": \"Weekly Pretest\", \"add\": \"Add a Monday pretest that gives each child a practice list of only the words they missed.\"}, {\"label\": \"Spelling Bee Club\", \"add\": \"Add spelling bee rounds where students type each word from a definition and a sentence.\"}, {\"label\": \"Spelling Rules\", \"add\": \"Add a rule tag to every word so I can see which spelling rule each class misses.\"}, {\"label\": \"Front Desk Hiring\", \"add\": \"Add a 20-word spelling check for applicants that emails the recruiter on a pass.\"}]}; </script></div></div><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script id='awb-quiz-data'> window.awbQuiz = {\"version\":1,\"type\":\"knowledge\",\"title\":\"Spelling Quiz: Can You Pick the Right Spelling of 8 Words?\",\"intro\":\"Eight words with doubled letters, silent letters, and tricky vowels. Pick the correct spelling for each; your score and a tip for every word show at the end.\",\"questions\":[{\"text\":\"The hotel can ___ 200 guests. Which spelling is correct?\",\"options\":[{\"text\":\"Accomodate\"},{\"text\":\"Accommodate\",\"correct\":true},{\"text\":\"Acommodate\"},{\"text\":\"Accommadate\"}],\"explanation\":\"Accommodate has two c's and two m's. Picture a room big enough to hold both pairs.\",\"source\":{\"url\":\"https://www.vocabulary.com/dictionary/accommodate\",\"quote\":\"If you accommodate, you are making an adjustment to suit a particular purpose\"}},{\"text\":\"Keep the raw chicken ___ from the salad. Which spelling is correct?\",\"options\":[{\"text\":\"Seperate\"},{\"text\":\"Separate\",\"correct\":true},{\"text\":\"Seperete\"},{\"text\":\"Separete\"}],\"explanation\":\"There is a rat in separate: sep, a, rat, e. The second letter after the p is an a, not an e.\",\"source\":{\"url\":\"https://www.vocabulary.com/dictionary/separate\",\"quote\":\"Things that are separate are kept apart from other things\"}},{\"text\":\"Food and water are ___ for every living thing. Which spelling is correct?\",\"options\":[{\"text\":\"Neccessary\"},{\"text\":\"Necessary\",\"correct\":true},{\"text\":\"Necesary\"},{\"text\":\"Neccesary\"}],\"explanation\":\"One c and two s's, like a shirt with one collar and two sleeves.\",\"source\":{\"url\":\"https://www.vocabulary.com/dictionary/necessary\",\"quote\":\"certain things are necessary for survival: food, water, shelter\"}},{\"text\":\"I will ___ be at the game on Saturday. Which spelling is correct?\",\"options\":[{\"text\":\"Definately\"},{\"text\":\"Definitely\",\"correct\":true},{\"text\":\"Definitly\"},{\"text\":\"Defanitely\"}],\"explanation\":\"Definitely is built on finite, so the letter after the n is an i, never an a.\",\"source\":{\"url\":\"https://www.vocabulary.com/dictionary/definitely\",\"quote\":\"Use definitely to describe something you\"}},{\"text\":\"The drummer kept a steady ___. Which spelling is correct?\",\"options\":[{\"text\":\"Rythm\"},{\"text\":\"Rhythm\",\"correct\":true},{\"text\":\"Rhythym\"},{\"text\":\"Rhthym\"}],\"explanation\":\"Rhythm uses y as its only vowel: r, h, y, t, h, m. The h appears twice.\",\"source\":{\"url\":\"https://www.vocabulary.com/dictionary/rhythm\",\"quote\":\"Use the noun rhythm to refer to the regular pattern of something in a cycle\"}},{\"text\":\"Did the mistake ___ you in front of the class? Which spelling is correct?\",\"options\":[{\"text\":\"Embarass\"},{\"text\":\"Embarrass\",\"correct\":true},{\"text\":\"Emberrass\"},{\"text\":\"Embaras\"}],\"explanation\":\"Embarrass doubles both the r and the s, which is the part people drop.\",\"source\":{\"url\":\"https://www.vocabulary.com/dictionary/embarrass\",\"quote\":\"If you embarrass someone, you make them feel self-conscious\"}},{\"text\":\"A solar eclipse is a rare ___. Which spelling is correct?\",\"options\":[{\"text\":\"Occurence\"},{\"text\":\"Occurrence\",\"correct\":true},{\"text\":\"Ocurrence\"},{\"text\":\"Occurrance\"}],\"explanation\":\"Two c's, two r's, and an ending of ence, not ance. The r doubles when occur takes the ending.\",\"source\":{\"url\":\"https://www.vocabulary.com/dictionary/occurrence\",\"quote\":\"An occurrence is an instance of something or a time when something happens\"}},{\"text\":\"Did you ___ my email this morning? Which spelling is correct?\",\"options\":[{\"text\":\"Recieve\"},{\"text\":\"Receive\",\"correct\":true},{\"text\":\"Receeve\"},{\"text\":\"Riceive\"}],\"explanation\":\"After a c, the e comes before the i, as in receive, ceiling, and receipt.\",\"source\":{\"url\":\"https://www.vocabulary.com/dictionary/receive\",\"quote\":\"Receive means to get or accept\"}}],\"results\":[{\"key\":\"keep-practicing\",\"title\":\"Keep Practicing\",\"description\":\"Each of these 8 words hides a trap that is easy to miss. Read the tip for each one you missed, write the word out three times, and take the quiz again tomorrow to see what stuck.\",\"min\":0,\"max\":3},{\"key\":\"solid-speller\",\"title\":\"Solid Speller\",\"description\":\"You know the common traps and missed a few doubled letters or vowel swaps. Check the tips for the words you missed; the pattern behind each one shows up in other words too.\",\"min\":4,\"max\":6},{\"key\":\"spelling-pro\",\"title\":\"Spelling Pro\",\"description\":\"You spotted the right spelling almost every time, doubled letters and all. Try writing your own list of tricky words and testing a friend, a class, or your team with it.\",\"min\":7,\"max\":8}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
